# Trivy ignores for the server image. Every entry needs a reason and an expiry (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
# Go stdlib CVEs in /usr/bin/pebble, which ships in the eclipse-temurin (Ubuntu) base image.
# Our container never runs it (ENTRYPOINT is java). Ubuntu had no fixed package on 2026-10-16;
# `apt-get upgrade` in the Dockerfile picks it up once released. Re-check by the expiry date.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-30
# Same binary (/usr/bin/pebble, Go stdlib crypto/x509), reported 2026-10-21; still no fixed Ubuntu package.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-30
